WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.930
Bright lights, slot machines, poker, blackjack....

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:16.700
Our minds have probably all just travelled
to Las Vegas.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.140
The city of sin… the place everyone thinks
of when we think of gambling.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.870
And that’s because it’s the world capital
of gambling, right?!

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.730
Well, it´s not!

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:31.870
Because the world’s real leading city of
gambling is not Las Vegas... but Macau.

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:37.030
Macau is an autonomous city situated in the
south of China, very close to Hong Kong.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:42.290
It’s so close to Hong Kong in fact that
the normal way to get to Macau is by very

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:47.910
fast ferries which connect the cities in just
over than an hour.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.420
Macao is a curious city.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:56.149
On the one hand, it is a small piece of Portugal
inside the chaotic and vibrant Asian south-west.

00:00:56.149 --> 00:01:02.290
On the other hand, it is a place where skyscrapers
and bold modern architecture are easy to find.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:08.790
The city’s landscape is dominated by an
enormous skyscraper with colourful crystals

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:14.069
in the shape of lotus flowers: the Grand Lisboa
Casino.

00:01:14.069 --> 00:01:20.880
Above all though, it is quite a messy city,
it’s all rather ramshackle and full of little

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.710
streets.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:30.579
Macau was the last European colony in continental
Asia and it remained so until very recent

00:01:30.579 --> 00:01:31.579
times.

00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:38.069
For centuries it was part of Portugal and
at the end of 1999 it was integrated in China.

00:01:38.069 --> 00:01:43.630
It was set up as a special administrative
region which allows for a “one country,

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:45.139
two systems” set up.

00:01:45.139 --> 00:01:50.229
These two cities (Hong Kong and Macau), even
though they belong to China, they keep (with

00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:56.399
some limitations) their own legislation, customs,
courts, currency and political institutions.

00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:00.579
In practical terms, they really work as if
they were different countries.

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:08.509
In Macau, Portuguese is even an official language.

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:14.970
But really Macau could be more considered
a gambling theme park than a city.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.930
Every year it receives more than 30 million
tourists.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:24.210
Yes, this tiny piece of land is one of the
world’s most visited places...

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.690
Why?

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:37.360
Because it is the only place where gambling
is permitted in China.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:42.340
Thanks to this, since its integration into
China up until 2014, this region has one of

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:46.000
the fastest periods of economic growth in
history.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:54.250
In little more than ten years, its GDP multiplied
by 10, growing from $5 billion to $55 billion.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:58.180
There was a key moment in this rapid growth
process: it was when the local government

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.630
gave the gambling industry free rein.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:10.810
In this very moment, huge multinational corporations
in

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:19.900
the gambling industry rushed to establish
themselves there, transforming Macau´s identity

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:20.900
forever.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:24.500
Today the city is known as the “Chinese
Las Vegas” for its high concentration of

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:28.240
casinos, but this is a ridiculous term.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.240
Dear viewers...

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.010
Macau is far far more than Las Vegas.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:40.350
In Macau’s 40 plus casinos, $29 billion
were invoiced in 2015, which is almost five

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.470
times more than Vegas.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.010
And guess what?

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:51.900
In 2013, it reached the astonishing amount
of $45 billion, which is almost the same amount

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:56.290
of money France receives from its entire tourism
industry.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.370
It is quite amazing.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:03.490
Gambling, lights, luxury shops, and, well,
still more lights...that´s Macau’s new,

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.180
and growing, identity.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.560
So, now you know!

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.819
From now on, every time you think of a slot
machine, poker or blackjack table, don´t

00:04:11.819 --> 00:04:15.490
think of Monte Carlo or Vegas, think of Macau.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:18.030
And there is no slowing down.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:22.620
Three new mega casinos, the result of multi-million
dollar investments have opened in the last

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:25.620
twelve months alone.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:31.979
At the end of 2015 the “Studio City” hotel
and casino was opened.

00:04:31.979 --> 00:04:38.520
This is a huge complex with a Hollywood atmosphere
whose opening saw the production of the most

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:44.319
expensive short film in history with a budget
of more than $70 million.

00:04:44.319 --> 00:04:49.979
It was directed by Martin Scorsese with important
lead roles played by Robert de Niro, Leonardo

00:04:49.979 --> 00:04:52.060
DiCaprio and Brad Pitt.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:05:02.020
What other hotel opening could possibly compare
to this?

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:09.650
More recently, in August 2016, the Wynn Palace
opened its doors.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:16.159
A luxurious hotel with more than 1,700 rooms
which cost its developers $4.2 billion dollars.

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:26.520
The most recent and the last to open has been
“The Parisian”, a new masterpiece by Las

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:30.270
Vegas Sands (the company belonging to wealthy
investor Sheldon Adelson).

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:37.800
This new complex is almost a city in itself
with 3000 rooms, a water park and, even, its

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:41.659
very own Eiffel Tower.

00:05:41.659 --> 00:05:50.809
And the openings still continue, the next
to open will be “The 13”, the most expensive

00:05:50.809 --> 00:05:52.180
super hotel in the world.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:57.729
Some of its rooms will cost between $50,000
and $100,000 dollars per night.

00:05:57.729 --> 00:05:59.999
No, this isn’t a mistake.

00:05:59.999 --> 00:06:04.720
Its guests will even have 30 Rolls Royce available
for them.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:08.120
Although they should be gifts for the guests,
given the prices.

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:13.439
Along with these new hotel casinos, the most
legendary in Macau are: The Galaxy, Grand

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:18.120
Lisboa, The City of Dreams, The Venetian,
the MGM, and many more.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:28.789
If they keep this up, the Strip in Las Vegas
will soon look like the work of an amateur.

00:06:28.789 --> 00:06:33.532
In Macau, more than 80% of governmental income
comes from casinos and the money the government

00:06:33.532 --> 00:06:38.029
gets is so abundant that, every year, it has
an enormous budget surplus.

00:06:38.029 --> 00:06:42.590
They are completely unfamiliar to the idea
of a public deficit, and, as you can imagine,

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:44.319
this means taxes are low.

00:06:44.319 --> 00:06:48.871
So, now you might be wondering: What does
the government do with all the surplus they

00:06:48.871 --> 00:06:49.871
obtain every year?

00:06:49.871 --> 00:06:57.139
Well, part of it is invested in infrastructure,
and a third of it is... wait for it... shared

00:06:57.139 --> 00:06:59.360
as dividends among the city residents.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:01.270
Yes, again, no mistake here.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:05.849
Since 2008, all the city’s inhabitants have
received part of the profit that the government

00:07:05.849 --> 00:07:07.379
gets from its casinos.

00:07:07.379 --> 00:07:11.949
For example, this year, the dividend was $1000
dollars per citizen....

00:07:11.949 --> 00:07:16.470
That means, for a family of four, they are
getting a check for $4000 dollars every single

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.930
year.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:19.930
Not bad ay?

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:24.039
And these are not the only benefits the citizens
receive - nearly one in every four jobs depends

00:07:24.039 --> 00:07:25.319
on the casino industry.

00:07:25.319 --> 00:07:31.279
So, low taxes, high employment rates, and,
on top of that, shared dividends.

00:07:31.279 --> 00:07:32.279
Pretty sweet.

00:07:32.279 --> 00:07:40.530
However, not everything is sunshine, lollipops
and rainbows.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:45.219
Most tourists in Macau, around two thirds,
come from continental China so the economy

00:07:45.219 --> 00:07:48.469
in this region is closely connected to China’s
economy.

00:07:48.469 --> 00:07:52.379
And if this wasn’t enough, Xi Jinping, the
President of China, started a war against

00:07:52.379 --> 00:07:55.289
public worker corruption in 2015.

00:07:55.289 --> 00:08:10.869
At that time, the economy 
of

00:08:10.869 --> 00:08:11.869
Macau collapsed.

00:08:11.869 --> 00:08:17.749
In a single year, gambling income fell by
40%, leading to the economy in Macau losing

00:08:17.749 --> 00:08:19.809
more than 20% of its GDP.

00:08:19.809 --> 00:08:23.470
The corrupt public workers in China had grown
accustomed to Macau’s casinos.

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:27.759
They could spend their ill-gotten money quite
easily, and spend time at red-carpet like

00:08:27.759 --> 00:08:34.370
events and, even, if lucky enough, they could
do some laundry… of the money variety.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:39.789
It’s not as if the whole industry depends
completely on them...

00:08:39.789 --> 00:08:44.410
But add in the Chinese economic slowdown and
the new controls established by the Chinese

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:49.040
government, and many of these VIP’s who
used to go Macau have stopped doing so...

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.350
at least for a little while.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:55.460
And well, half of Macau’s economy depends
directly on casinos.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:59.740
But, thanks to numerous investments, the good
condition of public finance, and the advantage

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:04.150
of being such an important tourist cluster,
both the social and economic effects have

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.150
been limited.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:09.730
The government keeps a comfortable surplus,
the unemployment rate is only 1.8% and family

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.100
incomes have not suffered.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:16.380
But one thing is true: As Xi Jinping said
it his last visit to the city, it is time

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:25.090
for diversification, and the government has
already presented a plan to tackle this.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:29.550
Macao will bet on family tourism, health tourism,
finance and the technological industry in

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:30.600
the next few years.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:33.660
This economy has already started to bounce
back.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:38.351
If the government’s plans become a reality,
Macau might become some kind of 21st Century

00:09:38.351 --> 00:09:40.260
Monaco in a few years.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.270
The city’s mistake was to put all eggs in
the one basket, leaving it too reliant on

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:48.350
one industry; instead of making it easy for
companies to form and attracting investment

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.329
from different industries.

00:09:50.329 --> 00:09:53.770
Something which happened in Atlantic City,
although with more serious consequences.

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:56.810
But that’s for another video...

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:58.500
What did you think about Macau?

